powerpagecomponent.content:
{
  "source": "{% comment %}
  The Tax check's notes, read-only, for a page that is not the Tax review itself
  (project owner, 2026-09-19). Include with:

    (% include 'OT Tax Notes' case_id: cid %)

  Q-TAX-03 "Case notes" is what the business calls the Tax notes. It is a question in a
  Tax-owned section, and AD-020 filters every review page to its own discipline, so an AQS
  checker reading a completed check and an adviser reading a remediation could not see it
  at all. Both are people the Tax checker was writing for.

  Nothing here is editable. A response belongs to the review that recorded it, and the Tax
  review is submitted and locked (BR-012, PP-11) by the time either of these pages is read.

  Only SUBMITTED Tax reviews are read. A draft Tax check is work in progress, and putting a
  half-written note in front of an adviser as though it were the finding would be worse than
  showing nothing.

  Every matching review is rendered, not just one. A case can carry more than one submitted
  Tax review - a recheck, or a regrade - and this Liquid applies no cross-entity order, so
  picking "the latest" would be picking an arbitrary one and calling it the latest. Each is
  labelled with its submission date instead, which is both honest and more useful; the
  ordinary case has exactly one.

  Renders nothing at all when there is no Tax note: a case may be AQS-only, or the Tax
  checker may simply have left the box empty, and an empty panel headed "Tax check notes"
  reads as a fault.
{% endcomment %}

{% if case_id and case_id != '' %}
  {% fetchxml ot_tax_notes %}
  <fetch>
    <entity name="al_response">
      <attribute name="al_responseid" />
      <attribute name="al_answertext" />
      <link-entity name="al_questionversion" from="al_questionversionid" to="al_questionversionid" alias="qv">
        <link-entity name="al_question" from="al_questionid" to="al_questionid" alias="q">
          <filter type="and">
            <condition attribute="al_questioncode" operator="eq" value="Q-TAX-03" />
          </filter>
        </link-entity>
      </link-entity>
      <link-entity name="al_reviewinstance" from="al_reviewinstanceid" to="al_reviewinstanceid" alias="ri">
        <attribute name="al_submittedon" />
        <attribute name="al_sequence" />
        <filter type="and">
          <condition attribute="al_outcomecaseid" operator="eq" value="{{ case_id | xml_escape }}" />
          <condition attribute="al_reviewtype" operator="eq" value="120910200" />
          <condition attribute="al_submittedon" operator="not-null" />
        </filter>
      </link-entity>
    </entity>
  </fetch>
  {% endfetchxml %}

  {% comment %}
    Counted before anything is drawn, so a case whose Tax checker left the box empty opens
    no panel. A response row can exist carrying a blank answer - the form writes one as soon
    as a question is touched - so the test is on the text, not on the row.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign ot_tax_note_count = 0 %}
  {% for r in ot_tax_notes.results.entities %}
    {% assign ot_note_text = r.al_answertext | strip %}
    {% if ot_note_text != '' %}
      {% assign ot_tax_note_count = ot_tax_note_count | plus: 1 %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}

  {% if ot_tax_note_count > 0 %}
  <section class="ot-card ot-tax-notes" aria-labelledby="ot-tax-notes-heading">
    <h2 class="ot-card__title" id="ot-tax-notes-heading">Tax check notes</h2>
    <p class="ot-tax-notes__intro">
      Recorded by the Tax checker when the Tax check was submitted. Read-only here.
    </p>
    {% for r in ot_tax_notes.results.entities %}
      {% assign ot_note_text = r.al_answertext | strip %}
      {% if ot_note_text != '' %}
      <div class="ot-tax-notes__item">
        {% if ot_tax_note_count > 1 %}
        <p class="ot-tax-notes__meta">
          Tax check submitted {{ r['ri.al_submittedon'] | date: 'dd MMM yyyy' | default: 'date not recorded' }}
        </p>
        {% endif %}
        <p class="ot-tax-notes__text">{{ ot_note_text | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
"
}
